  "worked_solution": "A function $h(x)$ is concave up over an interval $(a,b)$ if ${h}^{\u2033}(x)>0$ for all $x\\in (a,b).$\n\nOn the given graph of $y={h}^{\u2033}(x)$, we can see that ${h}^{\u2033}(x)>0$ on the intervals $(-3,0.75)$ and $(0.75,5).$ Therefore, the function $h(x)$ is concave up on the intervals $(-3,0.75)$ and $(0.75,5).$",
